1
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:04,796
[groans]
I think I went too hard.

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:06,965
My head's killing me. [groans]

3
00:00:07,049 --> 00:00:09,343
[both whooping]

4
00:00:09,801 --> 00:00:12,095
Well, do you wanna take off?

5
00:00:12,763 --> 00:00:14,223
[LUCY] Nah, I'll tough it out.

6
00:00:14,723 --> 00:00:15,891
[gags]

7
00:00:15,974 --> 00:00:17,768
No one's forcing you to do this.

8
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:20,270
I'm fine. If you go alone,
you might decide

9
00:00:20,354 --> 00:00:21,772
you like their team
more than ours!

10
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:24,650
Then you'll dump me because
I was too hungover to join!

11
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:25,817
[groans]

12
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:28,570
Quite an imagination you've got.

13
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:32,950
[MAKOTO] Hmm, seems like
an average cave to me.

14
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:35,410
It wasn't made
through average means, though.

15
00:00:35,494 --> 00:00:38,538
I did a little digging into it,
no pun intended.

16
00:00:38,622 --> 00:00:41,375
And apparently, it's man-made,
so it was probably used

17
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:43,752
as a mage's secret spot
to research spells.

18
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:47,047
But the place has been abandoned
for ages now.

19
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:48,215
Wow.

20
00:00:49,007 --> 00:00:52,010
[FUJIYAN]
Adventure beckons, my friends!

21
00:00:52,594 --> 00:00:55,055
[♪ opening theme song playing]

22
00:02:23,935 --> 00:02:26,104
[FUJIYAN]
Oh, absolutely magnificent.

23
00:02:26,188 --> 00:02:28,815
You don't often see
a dungeon like this one.

24
00:02:29,524 --> 00:02:32,361
[MAKOTO] I did expect it to be
a whole lot creepier.

25
00:02:33,403 --> 00:02:34,404
Uh?

26
00:02:35,113 --> 00:02:37,282
-A treasure chest!
-[Fujiyan gasps]

27
00:02:37,366 --> 00:02:40,160
There's a good chance
it's actually a trap, Lady Lucy.

28
00:02:41,745 --> 00:02:42,704
True.

29
00:02:43,455 --> 00:02:46,041
Uh, but I guess it was safe.

30
00:02:46,124 --> 00:02:47,834
-[all sigh]
-[Lucy gasps]

31
00:02:48,835 --> 00:02:51,838
Pretty! I bet it'd sell
for a small fortune!

32
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:53,632
-Uh?
-[rumbling]

33
00:02:53,715 --> 00:02:55,675
[all gasping]

34
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:58,720
-[NINA] We have company.
-[golems growling]

35
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:00,597
[LUCY] Wood golems.

36
00:03:01,223 --> 00:03:04,101
That's kind of perfect.
All wood things burn.

37
00:03:04,184 --> 00:03:05,769
Don't cast fire spells
in a cave!

38
00:03:05,852 --> 00:03:06,937
Why?

39
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:09,189
-Fire is what I do.
-There's no space,

40
00:03:09,272 --> 00:03:11,274
and I'd rather
not get burned again.

41
00:03:12,067 --> 00:03:13,568
Then allow me to clear the way.

42
00:03:13,652 --> 00:03:15,362
[FUJIYAN]
Have at them, Lady Nina!

43
00:03:15,445 --> 00:03:16,905
♪

44
00:03:16,988 --> 00:03:18,490
[grunts]

45
00:03:19,866 --> 00:03:20,951
Bare-handed?

46
00:03:21,034 --> 00:03:23,120
As one expects
of martial artists.

47
00:03:23,954 --> 00:03:24,913
[Nina gasps]

48
00:03:25,664 --> 00:03:26,832
[yells]

49
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:30,627
[LUCY]
She really kicks golem butt.

50
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:32,629
Here's more!

51
00:03:32,713 --> 00:03:33,672
[grunts]

52
00:03:36,758 --> 00:03:38,552
Now, fall!

53
00:03:39,678 --> 00:03:41,263
[growling]

54
00:03:42,013 --> 00:03:44,141
Whoa, that's ground magic.

55
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:45,350
♪

56
00:03:50,021 --> 00:03:51,690
Impressive work.

57
00:03:52,315 --> 00:03:54,317
But that's a Silver-rank
for you.

58
00:03:56,111 --> 00:03:58,864
So, Nina can use magic
without chanting, too.

59
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:01,658
Not quite. The takedown you saw
was accomplished

60
00:04:01,742 --> 00:04:03,785
-with a magic combat technique.
-What?

61
00:04:03,869 --> 00:04:05,954
It involves
fusing magical attacks

62
00:04:06,037 --> 00:04:07,080
into physical ones,

63
00:04:07,164 --> 00:04:08,790
creating a balanced
fighting style.

64
00:04:08,874 --> 00:04:11,042
Mastering traditional spells
would be much easier.

65
00:04:12,127 --> 00:04:14,588
Are you ready to move on?
[sighs contentedly]

66
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:15,964
[thudding]

67
00:04:16,047 --> 00:04:16,923
[MAKOTO] Golem!

68
00:04:17,007 --> 00:04:18,550
Another golem.

69
00:04:18,633 --> 00:04:19,885
-[grunts]
-[MAKOTO] Yup.

70
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:22,471
Just wood golems everywhere.

71
00:04:22,554 --> 00:04:23,472
Yeah.

72
00:04:24,431 --> 00:04:25,474
[Makoto gasps]

73
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:28,560
I sense a strong monster
down that way.

74
00:04:28,643 --> 00:04:29,728
[all gasp]

75
00:04:30,729 --> 00:04:31,772
[exhales]

76
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:34,691
[MAKOTO] There it is.

77
00:04:35,442 --> 00:04:36,735
[LUCY] A chimera!

78
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:37,944
What do you say?

79
00:04:38,028 --> 00:04:40,030
You think it's time
for an epic battle?

80
00:04:40,113 --> 00:04:41,990
Have patience, if you please.

81
00:04:42,073 --> 00:04:45,243
No sense rushing ahead
when we can appraise it.

82
00:04:45,786 --> 00:04:48,205
Uh-huh! It is indeed a chimera.

83
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:50,290
One with a weakness to fire.

84
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:53,877
-And, luckily, you guys have me!
-[FUJIYAN] I wasn't finished!

85
00:04:54,586 --> 00:04:55,837
[LUCY]
What's the issue this time?

86
00:04:55,921 --> 00:04:59,424
It was created back in year 10,
before salvation.

87
00:04:59,508 --> 00:05:00,842
Thus, in other words,

88
00:05:00,926 --> 00:05:03,136
we would be up against
a 1,000-year-old monster.

89
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:04,846
-[gasps]
-No, it's that old?

90
00:05:04,930 --> 00:05:06,848
[NINA]
I'm glad you checked, boss.

91
00:05:06,932 --> 00:05:08,767
[LUCY] You'd never know
by looking.

92
00:05:08,850 --> 00:05:10,185
Why does that matter?

93
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:12,229
[NINA] Monsters
from way back when

94
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:14,689
were influenced
by the Great Demon Lord.

95
00:05:14,773 --> 00:05:16,358
They make the ones
you'd find nowadays

96
00:05:16,441 --> 00:05:17,901
look like house pets.

97
00:05:18,735 --> 00:05:20,529
[LUCY] Many veteran adventurers
have challenged

98
00:05:20,612 --> 00:05:22,697
what they thought
was a normal monster,

99
00:05:22,781 --> 00:05:24,908
only to be completely decimated.

100
00:05:25,534 --> 00:05:28,286
Although,
none of them had a Nina or Lucy

101
00:05:28,370 --> 00:05:29,496
to keep them safe.

102
00:05:29,829 --> 00:05:31,206
-[both chuckle]
-[MAKOTO] Hmm.

103
00:05:31,289 --> 00:05:33,083
[NINA] Plus,
it's protecting that gate.

104
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:35,877
Guard monsters can only
move so far from their posts.

105
00:05:36,461 --> 00:05:37,671
Let's try fighting it,

106
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:39,673
and if we decide it's too much,
we can just run.

107
00:05:39,756 --> 00:05:42,717
Hm. Lest we forget,
I am currently equipped

108
00:05:42,801 --> 00:05:44,928
with an Escape Card
at the ready as well.

109
00:05:45,011 --> 00:05:46,555
In that case, sure.

110
00:05:46,638 --> 00:05:48,515
[snoring softly]

111
00:05:50,892 --> 00:05:52,686
[MAKOTO]
I'll back up Nina from here.

112
00:05:53,144 --> 00:05:55,939
Lucy, you got us covered
with some fire?

113
00:05:56,022 --> 00:05:57,065
Yeah, of course.

114
00:05:57,148 --> 00:05:58,191
-O Goddess Sol...
-All right, gang!

115
00:05:58,275 --> 00:05:59,526
Give it all you've got!

116
00:05:59,609 --> 00:06:00,986
-...who governs the flame.
-But ladies first.

117
00:06:01,861 --> 00:06:03,321
♪

118
00:06:03,405 --> 00:06:06,032
[roaring]

119
00:06:06,866 --> 00:06:09,077
[Nina grunts, yells]

120
00:06:10,954 --> 00:06:12,831
Saagya-tah-wah-sah-toneday.

121
00:06:13,832 --> 00:06:14,833
[MAKOTO] Nice!

122
00:06:14,916 --> 00:06:16,418
That's all I need.

123
00:06:17,043 --> 00:06:19,838
Water Magic. Ice. Arrow Strike!

124
00:06:21,214 --> 00:06:22,674
Man, still weak.

125
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:24,092
It isn't over yet!

126
00:06:25,176 --> 00:06:26,177
[grunting]

127
00:06:28,305 --> 00:06:29,389
[yells]

128
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:32,142
[gasps]

129
00:06:32,851 --> 00:06:35,395
That was a solid attack,
but it's barely fazed.

130
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:36,855
Talk about stubborn.

131
00:06:37,522 --> 00:06:38,607
New plan?

132
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:40,150
Let's stick with the old one,

133
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:42,360
but let's attack it
at the same time.

134
00:06:42,444 --> 00:06:43,653
[MAKOTO] Got it.

135
00:06:43,737 --> 00:06:45,614
Make sure to aim
for the lion head.

136
00:06:45,697 --> 00:06:47,157
Roger that.

137
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:49,451
Water Magic: Ice Bullet!

138
00:06:49,534 --> 00:06:50,410
[grunts]

139
00:06:51,995 --> 00:06:54,289
[Nina grunts, yells]

140
00:06:58,710 --> 00:06:59,753
Is it down?

141
00:07:05,342 --> 00:07:07,010
[growling]

142
00:07:07,594 --> 00:07:10,305
-Guess it's game for more.
-Great.

143
00:07:10,388 --> 00:07:12,265
I think it's my turn!

144
00:07:12,891 --> 00:07:14,643
Well then, bring on the fire!

145
00:07:14,726 --> 00:07:15,769
[LUCY] I always do!

146
00:07:16,269 --> 00:07:19,022
Come forth, Fireball!

147
00:07:23,234 --> 00:07:26,112
-[Lucy groans]
-We're falling back, now!

148
00:07:26,738 --> 00:07:28,531
[snoring]

149
00:07:28,615 --> 00:07:30,158
[NINA] Do we call it quits?

150
00:07:30,241 --> 00:07:32,243
If we can't find a way
past the chimera's gate,

151
00:07:32,327 --> 00:07:33,411
we'll have to leave.

152
00:07:33,495 --> 00:07:36,081
Yeah. But the chimera
didn't attack us

153
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:38,041
until we got close, did it?

154
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:41,419
I say we try it again
and just keep our distance.

155
00:07:41,503 --> 00:07:42,587
[MAKOTO] Worth a shot.

156
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:45,840
That makes Lucy's magic
even more crucial, though.

157
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:49,094
How about I block
the chimera's line of sight

158
00:07:49,177 --> 00:07:50,720
and you draw
its attention, Nina?

159
00:07:50,804 --> 00:07:52,305
[NINA] My specialty.

160
00:07:52,389 --> 00:07:54,808
Okay. It's round two.

161
00:07:54,891 --> 00:07:56,851
Right. Yay.

162
00:07:57,352 --> 00:07:59,312
Think it's time,
so get the thing.

163
00:07:59,396 --> 00:08:01,564
-[FUJIYAN] You want it already?
-Yup.

164
00:08:01,648 --> 00:08:02,941
What's "the thing?"

165
00:08:03,525 --> 00:08:06,069
Storage: Withdraw!

166
00:08:14,285 --> 00:08:15,537
Water?

167
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:18,206
Fujiyan can hold anything
with his Storage skill,

168
00:08:18,289 --> 00:08:20,208
so I thought,
"Hey, let's take a pond."

169
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,002
[LUCY] Smart move.
Now, you're set.

170
00:08:23,086 --> 00:08:25,005
I hope so. Are you?

171
00:08:25,422 --> 00:08:29,884
Um, well, kind of.
I might botch the shot again.

172
00:08:29,968 --> 00:08:31,386
I'll support you either way.

173
00:08:31,469 --> 00:08:33,638
-Just give it your best shot.
-Hmm.

174
00:08:33,722 --> 00:08:35,056
Right.

175
00:08:35,724 --> 00:08:38,017
-I can do this.
-Hmm.

176
00:08:38,101 --> 00:08:40,520
Round two, electric boogaloo!

177
00:08:41,104 --> 00:08:43,648
Water Magic: Fog!

178
00:08:43,732 --> 00:08:44,733
♪

179
00:08:49,571 --> 00:08:52,157
[roaring]

180
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:55,201
[grunts, yells]

181
00:08:56,244 --> 00:08:57,996
[groaning]

182
00:08:59,998 --> 00:09:01,166
Lucy!

183
00:09:01,249 --> 00:09:03,168
Now, Fire Arrow!

184
00:09:05,128 --> 00:09:06,254
Water Magic.

185
00:09:07,589 --> 00:09:08,923
It veered away!

186
00:09:09,007 --> 00:09:10,425
Surging Flow!

187
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:13,595
[growling]

188
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:16,681
[bellows]

189
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:19,642
[NINA] Ground Magic. Huge Rock!

190
00:09:21,978 --> 00:09:24,647
And shoot!

191
00:09:33,114 --> 00:09:35,617
[chimera groans softly]

192
00:09:38,203 --> 00:09:39,412
[sighs]

193
00:09:40,288 --> 00:09:41,414
[gasps]

194
00:09:41,498 --> 00:09:42,415
[squeals]

195
00:09:42,499 --> 00:09:45,418
No way! You guys, we won!

196
00:09:45,502 --> 00:09:47,420
[laughing]

197
00:09:47,796 --> 00:09:49,172
[footsteps]

198
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:52,717
[LUCY] What an incredibly
spacious room.

199
00:09:52,801 --> 00:09:55,762
The main power chamber,
if I had to guess.

200
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:58,139
[MAKOTO] Based on this boulder?

201
00:09:58,556 --> 00:09:59,724
[NINA]
Well, this boulder might be

202
00:09:59,808 --> 00:10:00,975
the main power source.

203
00:10:01,059 --> 00:10:03,561
Correct. So, the energy
it contains within

204
00:10:03,645 --> 00:10:05,396
must be immense,
to say the least,

205
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:08,107
given how it fueled a dungeon
for over 1,000 years.

206
00:10:08,566 --> 00:10:09,943
I suppose so.

207
00:10:10,944 --> 00:10:11,986
[yelps]

208
00:10:12,070 --> 00:10:13,947
I just got zapped by it!

209
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:16,825
That's what you get when
you touch mysterious things.

210
00:10:17,492 --> 00:10:19,244
Always appraise first.

211
00:10:20,453 --> 00:10:23,248
Unbelievable!
It could generate enough energy

212
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:25,583
to power the entire city
of Macallan!

213
00:10:26,125 --> 00:10:27,585
And what's even more astounding

214
00:10:27,669 --> 00:10:29,879
is what this huge rock
actually is!

215
00:10:29,963 --> 00:10:31,464
-[rumbling]
-[yelps]

216
00:10:32,006 --> 00:10:32,966
[Nina and Lucy yelp]

217
00:10:33,049 --> 00:10:34,717
Is the rock getting up?

218
00:10:34,801 --> 00:10:36,219
♪

219
00:10:43,476 --> 00:10:45,144
[LUCY] A giant?

220
00:10:45,228 --> 00:10:48,898
[MAKOTO]
Uh... yeah, a giant problem.

221
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:53,069
[TITANEA] Children of man,

222
00:10:53,528 --> 00:10:56,948
tell me, who among you
broke the seal?

223
00:10:57,031 --> 00:10:59,492
-[MAKOTO] Uh...
-[Lucy grunts]

224
00:10:59,576 --> 00:11:02,495
[FUJIYAN] Uh...
um, it was I, sir.

225
00:11:02,579 --> 00:11:05,540
I believe I did it
using my Appraise skill.

226
00:11:05,999 --> 00:11:09,502
[TITANEA] I was placed
under a petrification spell.

227
00:11:09,586 --> 00:11:13,840
Only the Divine Eye could have
uncovered my true identity.

228
00:11:13,923 --> 00:11:18,261
For not even the gods' disguises
can deceive its gaze.

229
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:21,514
Oh, yeah? Is your Appraise skill
that fancy?

230
00:11:21,598 --> 00:11:23,182
No, certainly not!

231
00:11:23,266 --> 00:11:25,018
The gods could
deceive me all day!

232
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:26,644
[TITANEA] I see.

233
00:11:26,728 --> 00:11:30,440
Regardless, the seal was broken,
thanks to you.

234
00:11:31,024 --> 00:11:35,612
And strangely I do sense
someone's will at work.

235
00:11:36,237 --> 00:11:38,239
Now, I hunger.

236
00:11:38,323 --> 00:11:39,991
Uh? Gotta run.

237
00:11:40,074 --> 00:11:42,243
-[all gasp]
-[TITANEA] Leaving so soon?

238
00:11:42,327 --> 00:11:43,411
Ah, crap.

239
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:45,496
I'll distract him
while you guys go!

240
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:46,998
[FUJIYAN] Uh, Lady Nina!

241
00:11:48,374 --> 00:11:49,500
[Nina yells]

242
00:11:53,630 --> 00:11:55,256
[all gasping]

243
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:58,509
[FUJIYAN] Lady Nina,
please stay with me.

244
00:11:58,593 --> 00:11:59,677
[gasps]

245
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:02,347
You recite a chant
while I buy you some time,

246
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:04,057
-but hurry.
-Right, chanting!

247
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:07,852
O Goddess Sol, protector of life
who governs the flame,

248
00:12:07,936 --> 00:12:09,646
today is the day of beginnings,

249
00:12:09,729 --> 00:12:11,940
the day of genesis
whence you pronounced,

250
00:12:12,023 --> 00:12:14,651
"Let the fires of creation
illuminate the world."

251
00:12:15,318 --> 00:12:16,653
[MAKOTO] What now?

252
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:18,029
[chimes]

253
00:12:18,112 --> 00:12:20,323
[MAKOTO]
Titanea? So not a giant.

254
00:12:22,825 --> 00:12:24,911
Lucy's spell is still buffering.

255
00:12:25,411 --> 00:12:28,081
And Fujiyan's focused on Nina.

256
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:31,042
But it's fine,
I'm used to soloing.

257
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:34,587
Saagya-tah-wah-sah-toneday.

258
00:12:34,671 --> 00:12:35,797
[Titanea grunts]

259
00:12:37,674 --> 00:12:40,385
Water Magic: Fog!

260
00:12:41,386 --> 00:12:42,679
[Titanea grunts]

261
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:46,057
[MAKOTO] Any words of wisdom,
O benevolent goddess?

262
00:12:48,518 --> 00:12:50,603
And you're normally
so chatty, too.

263
00:12:50,687 --> 00:12:51,562
Stealth.

264
00:12:52,939 --> 00:12:54,607
-[TITANEA] I think not.
-[gasps]

265
00:12:54,691 --> 00:12:55,900
[MAKOTO] Dodge!

266
00:12:56,693 --> 00:12:57,819
He saw me?

267
00:12:59,445 --> 00:13:01,114
[grunting]

268
00:13:01,197 --> 00:13:02,615
[gasps]

269
00:13:02,699 --> 00:13:04,409
-Dodge!
-May they burn bright

270
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:05,868
in accordance with your will.

271
00:13:05,952 --> 00:13:07,620
[Titanea grunts]

272
00:13:09,706 --> 00:13:13,001
[TITANEA] That dagger,
where did you get it?

273
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:17,839
Such power
must not be used by a human.

274
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:19,007
[grunts, gasps]

275
00:13:19,966 --> 00:13:21,467
[Makoto struggling]

276
00:13:21,551 --> 00:13:23,011
Makoto, no!

277
00:13:23,094 --> 00:13:25,471
[Titanea growls]

278
00:13:25,555 --> 00:13:27,265
[grunting]

279
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:28,516
[NOAH] Not so fast.

280
00:13:29,434 --> 00:13:33,104
[TITANEA] Wait.
Is that you, Lady Noah?

281
00:13:33,187 --> 00:13:36,941
[NOAH] Yep, sure is, pops.
And that boy is my believer.

282
00:13:37,025 --> 00:13:39,777
[TITANEA] Oh!
Well, good for you.

283
00:13:39,861 --> 00:13:41,320
Thanks, "pops."

284
00:13:41,404 --> 00:13:43,406
[TITANEA]
My apologies, young man.

285
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:45,033
[grunts, thuds]

286
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:46,325
[groans]

287
00:13:46,409 --> 00:13:48,077
[NOAH] Be grateful, Makoto.

288
00:13:48,161 --> 00:13:51,289
-Your faith in me saved you.
-What?

289
00:13:51,372 --> 00:13:53,791
[TITANEA]
If you are Lady Noah's believer,

290
00:13:53,875 --> 00:13:55,585
I shall think of you as family.

291
00:13:55,668 --> 00:13:56,711
[MAKOTO] So, you're acquainted

292
00:13:56,794 --> 00:13:58,463
with this man-eating pile
of rocks?

293
00:13:58,546 --> 00:14:00,423
[NOAH]
Don't be such a drama queen.

294
00:14:00,506 --> 00:14:02,467
He'd never actually eat people.

295
00:14:04,469 --> 00:14:06,429
Well, he seemed
pretty dead set on turning me

296
00:14:06,512 --> 00:14:08,014
into a snack just now.

297
00:14:08,097 --> 00:14:10,892
[TITANEA] I was startled
after you suddenly attacked me.

298
00:14:11,309 --> 00:14:13,686
They called it
self-defense, child.

299
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:16,397
[MAKOTO]
Someone's feeling guilty.

300
00:14:16,481 --> 00:14:19,484
[NOAH] Ah, sorry, fellas.
My time's up.

301
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:21,861
The rest is in your hands.

302
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:24,280
Well, that was
quicker than usual.

303
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:29,035
Speaking of hands,
uh, sorry, about your finger.

304
00:14:30,536 --> 00:14:32,872
I don't suppose
you can just stick it back on?

305
00:14:33,331 --> 00:14:37,376
[TITANEA] No, but it will regrow
in 10,000 years.

306
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:39,462
Hey,
then that's a load off my mind.

307
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:40,630
Sort of.

308
00:14:41,589 --> 00:14:44,050
What's going on?
Are you two friends?

309
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:47,053
Yeah, basically.

310
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:48,596
♪

311
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:49,597
[FUJIYAN] Enjoy.

312
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:52,058
There's plenty more!
So, please eat your fill!

313
00:14:52,141 --> 00:14:54,268
[TITANEA] How nostalgic!

314
00:14:54,352 --> 00:14:58,398
To think I may once again
partake of the land's bounty!

315
00:14:59,190 --> 00:15:02,068
What a strange day.
I can't believe he's friends

316
00:15:02,151 --> 00:15:04,237
with the evil god Lord Tackie
so reveres.

317
00:15:04,821 --> 00:15:07,115
Wait, Makoto reveres
an evil god?

318
00:15:07,198 --> 00:15:08,407
Why didn't I know this sooner?

319
00:15:08,491 --> 00:15:10,076
'Cause I never mentioned it.

320
00:15:10,159 --> 00:15:13,204
[TITANEA] We Titanea exist
to serve as guardians

321
00:15:13,287 --> 00:15:16,249
for Lady Noah
and the other mighty Titans.

322
00:15:16,332 --> 00:15:19,919
After I was bested
in the war 15 million years ago,

323
00:15:20,002 --> 00:15:21,921
my foes placed me
under that seal.

324
00:15:22,922 --> 00:15:25,633
But I was finally freed,
thanks to you,

325
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:28,553
and you extended
your kindness further still

326
00:15:28,636 --> 00:15:30,346
by offering me food.

327
00:15:30,429 --> 00:15:32,390
Is there anything you desire?

328
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:36,102
-[FUJIYAN] Uh, anything at all?
-Yes.

329
00:15:36,769 --> 00:15:37,895
[FUJIYAN] Hmm.

330
00:15:38,855 --> 00:15:40,148
Great Titanea,

331
00:15:40,231 --> 00:15:43,025
might I receive
this severed finger of yours?

332
00:15:43,109 --> 00:15:44,360
[both groan]

333
00:15:44,443 --> 00:15:46,195
But it's perfectly fine
if the answer is no.

334
00:15:46,279 --> 00:15:49,782
[TITANEA] Should such a thing
make you happy, please take it.

335
00:15:49,866 --> 00:15:51,534
[FUJIYAN] I am so very grateful.

336
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:53,244
[MAKOTO] I don't even wanna know
why he wants that.

337
00:15:53,744 --> 00:15:55,288
[TITANEA] As for the red one,

338
00:15:55,371 --> 00:15:57,540
it would seem
controlling your magic

339
00:15:57,623 --> 00:15:59,584
is a difficult task for you.

340
00:15:59,667 --> 00:16:01,752
I'm surprised you could tell.

341
00:16:01,836 --> 00:16:04,630
[TITANEA]
Lend me your staff for a moment.

342
00:16:11,012 --> 00:16:11,971
[gasps]

343
00:16:12,430 --> 00:16:15,099
[TITANEA] Ground magic
will be easier to use now.

344
00:16:15,183 --> 00:16:16,893
Wow! Really?

345
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:19,478
Then, O Keres,
goddess of earth...

346
00:16:19,562 --> 00:16:21,731
[TITANEA]
Next is the Beastfolk child.

347
00:16:21,814 --> 00:16:23,399
-[NINA] Huh?
-[LUCY] The one strong...

348
00:16:23,482 --> 00:16:25,943
[TITANEA] I was wrong
to cause you harm.

349
00:16:26,027 --> 00:16:27,904
As penance for my misdeed,

350
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:31,157
I shall bestow upon you
the Titanea's blessing.

351
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:33,201
[Nina gasps]

352
00:16:33,659 --> 00:16:35,703
Whoa! Yeah.

353
00:16:35,786 --> 00:16:38,164
I feel power
welling up deep inside me.

354
00:16:38,247 --> 00:16:40,791
-[grunts]
-[rumbling]

355
00:16:40,875 --> 00:16:43,336
Sheesh! You could destroy
a whole building with that!

356
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:44,712
I could?

357
00:16:44,795 --> 00:16:46,297
-[LUCY] Ooh, now, me!
-[BOTH] Huh?

358
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:49,091
[LUCY] Ground Magic, shift!
Rock Bullet!

359
00:16:49,175 --> 00:16:50,343
[gasps]

360
00:16:50,426 --> 00:16:52,011
Oh, my goodness!

361
00:16:53,888 --> 00:16:55,097
Back during our training,

362
00:16:55,181 --> 00:16:57,308
she couldn't cast
a single ground magic spell.

363
00:16:57,391 --> 00:16:59,268
-Ah, I'm so sorry.
-Though, she could use

364
00:16:59,352 --> 00:17:01,604
-some control.
-Eh, I dodged in time.

365
00:17:01,687 --> 00:17:05,066
[MAKOTO] Lucky them.
Do I get a cool present, too?

366
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:08,319
[TITANEA] You received
Lady Noah's blessing

367
00:17:08,402 --> 00:17:11,614
and a divine treasure,
yet you yearn for more?

368
00:17:11,697 --> 00:17:14,909
Desire too great
will surely bring you ruin.

369
00:17:14,992 --> 00:17:16,702
[MAKOTO]
Uh, another mind-reader.

370
00:17:16,786 --> 00:17:20,456
[TITANEA] Well, no matter.
What is it you wish?

371
00:17:22,375 --> 00:17:25,086
I wish to save Lady Noah
from the Seafloor Temple.

372
00:17:25,169 --> 00:17:26,087
♪

373
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:28,130
[TITANEA] I cannot grant that.

374
00:17:28,214 --> 00:17:30,299
But wishing
for our master's benefit

375
00:17:30,383 --> 00:17:33,844
before your own
is truly admirable.

376
00:17:33,928 --> 00:17:36,555
So, I shall impart some advice.

377
00:17:36,639 --> 00:17:39,308
Take heed
when speaking Elementali.

378
00:17:39,392 --> 00:17:43,562
It is a tongue whose power
must always be respected.

379
00:17:43,646 --> 00:17:48,025
If you wish to borrow
the strength of the elementals

380
00:17:48,109 --> 00:17:52,321
visit them, converse with them,
and befriend them.

381
00:17:52,405 --> 00:17:53,864
I would if I could.

382
00:17:53,948 --> 00:17:56,575
Thing is, I don't have the power
to see elementals.

383
00:17:57,785 --> 00:17:59,370
-Uh?
-[TITANEA] Behold.

384
00:17:59,453 --> 00:18:00,830
[gasps]

385
00:18:02,123 --> 00:18:04,208
[MAKOTO] Is this mana?

386
00:18:05,001 --> 00:18:06,127
Amazing.

387
00:18:06,669 --> 00:18:07,795
[gasps]

388
00:18:08,379 --> 00:18:12,258
The flocks of elementals
are mana itself.

389
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:13,342
I see.

390
00:18:14,135 --> 00:18:15,761
I've gotta ask for their help.

391
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:17,805
Thinking I could
just command them

392
00:18:17,888 --> 00:18:19,640
when I felt like
it was ridiculous.

393
00:18:19,724 --> 00:18:21,642
[TITANEA] Yes, you understand.

394
00:18:21,726 --> 00:18:24,812
Those without talent
cannot see them.

395
00:18:24,895 --> 00:18:28,733
And it appears the elementals
are quite fond of you.

396
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:30,860
Strive to improve.

397
00:18:32,611 --> 00:18:36,073
With that, I bid you farewell.

398
00:18:39,410 --> 00:18:41,287
[MAKOTO] "Strive to improve."

399
00:18:41,579 --> 00:18:42,747
[scoffs]

400
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:44,373
-[insects trilling]
-[distant barking]

401
00:18:46,584 --> 00:18:48,169
[MAKOTO] Easier said than done.

402
00:18:49,003 --> 00:18:52,173
I'm capped out,
nothing left for me to unlock.

403
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:55,760
[sighs] So what exactly
do I strive to improve?

404
00:18:57,219 --> 00:18:59,263
My magic mastery is 99.

405
00:19:00,639 --> 00:19:03,267
I should be happy
about capping it out.

406
00:19:04,185 --> 00:19:05,269
But I'm not.

407
00:19:07,813 --> 00:19:09,774
Is this as far as I go?

408
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,651
Uh...

409
00:19:12,735 --> 00:19:14,028
-[Noah grunts]
-[gasps]

410
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:15,446
Don't do that!

411
00:19:15,821 --> 00:19:17,406
Hey, my one believer,

412
00:19:17,490 --> 00:19:19,617
if that's what
you still consider yourself.

413
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:22,286
Hard to tell when you won't let
your goddess do her job.

414
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:24,455
But I give you offerings.

415
00:19:24,538 --> 00:19:27,416
That's not the only thing.
Those are just perks, you idiot.

416
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:30,878
FYI, a goddess' sacred duty
is to guide her lambs

417
00:19:30,961 --> 00:19:32,713
-whenever they lose their way.
-Okay.

418
00:19:32,797 --> 00:19:34,173
Lately,
you've been moping around

419
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:35,758
and just worrying yourself sick.

420
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:38,469
That's when you're supposed
to come to me for help, dummy.

421
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:40,638
My face is right in your chest.

422
00:19:40,721 --> 00:19:42,181
Yeah, you're welcome.

423
00:19:42,264 --> 00:19:43,808
[Noah sighs]

424
00:19:43,891 --> 00:19:46,227
Why won't you let me guide
my little lamb?

425
00:19:46,310 --> 00:19:49,271
Well, relying on divine grace
is kinda shameless.

426
00:19:49,355 --> 00:19:51,190
So is begging you,
but here I am.

427
00:19:52,066 --> 00:19:54,151
Now, pass me your Soul Book
real quick.

428
00:19:54,235 --> 00:19:55,403
Oh.

429
00:19:56,070 --> 00:19:57,488
[MAKOTO] Here you go.

430
00:19:58,280 --> 00:20:00,241
Just the tiniest little tweak.

431
00:20:03,577 --> 00:20:05,955
-There!
-[gasps]

432
00:20:06,038 --> 00:20:08,582
[MAKOTO] Magic Mastery 103?

433
00:20:08,666 --> 00:20:09,750
But why?

434
00:20:09,834 --> 00:20:12,169
Because you, Makoto,
are the type of guy

435
00:20:12,253 --> 00:20:14,755
who maxes out his level
in all RPGs.

436
00:20:14,839 --> 00:20:17,216
So you worked and eventually
capped your mastery,

437
00:20:17,299 --> 00:20:19,301
which left you
with major burnout.

438
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:22,012
Guess you're sharper
than I thought you were.

439
00:20:22,096 --> 00:20:23,556
[chuckles] Yes, well,

440
00:20:23,639 --> 00:20:25,850
maybe you should
remember that next time.

441
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:28,769
Same goes for this
special bit of information, too.

442
00:20:28,853 --> 00:20:31,730
As soon as your mastery level
surpasses 105,

443
00:20:31,814 --> 00:20:32,982
you'll see elementals.

444
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:35,276
Whoa, I'm pretty close then.

445
00:20:35,359 --> 00:20:36,527
That's right!

446
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:38,779
And your spark's back
with a vengeance!

447
00:20:38,863 --> 00:20:41,115
Totally.
Thanks for relighting it.

448
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:42,992
Always happy to help a lamb.

449
00:20:43,075 --> 00:20:46,078
Just keep on working hard.
See you around.

450
00:20:46,579 --> 00:20:48,539
-Oh, wait.
-Huh?

451
00:20:48,622 --> 00:20:50,999
Modifying a Soul Book
is against the rules.

452
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:52,084
If you get caught,

453
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:54,170
the inquisitors
will have your neck on a rope.

454
00:20:54,253 --> 00:20:56,922
Did you sentence me to death?

455
00:20:57,006 --> 00:20:58,799
The church decided
the highest value

456
00:20:58,883 --> 00:21:01,010
for Soul Books is 99
on a random whim.

457
00:21:01,093 --> 00:21:02,094
But the reality

458
00:21:02,178 --> 00:21:04,054
is the mastery limit
does not exist.

459
00:21:04,138 --> 00:21:06,640
Now, yours shows the real one
'cause I tweaked it.

460
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:09,143
If Highland
or the Church of Roses sees,

461
00:21:09,226 --> 00:21:10,644
they're sure
to brand you a heretic

462
00:21:10,728 --> 00:21:12,646
and arrange an execution
in your honor.

463
00:21:13,773 --> 00:21:15,941
Make sense? Oop, I gotta
get going, time's up!

464
00:21:16,025 --> 00:21:17,860
-Nope, denied!
-Oh?

465
00:21:17,943 --> 00:21:20,196
Oh, you want me to stay
and chat with you?

466
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:24,408
Well, a quality conversation
with you does sound nice, yeah.

467
00:21:24,492 --> 00:21:27,161
[chuckles] Look at you,
getting sweeter by the day.

468
00:21:27,244 --> 00:21:30,206
You might end up sweet
on your goddess at this rate.

469
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:31,957
I don't like this. Please stop.

470
00:21:32,458 --> 00:21:35,294
[Noah chuckles]
One last thing before I go.

471
00:21:36,045 --> 00:21:37,588
I want you to make your way

472
00:21:37,671 --> 00:21:39,548
to the great maze
of Labyrinthos.

473
00:21:39,632 --> 00:21:40,925
[MAKOTO] Huh?

474
00:21:41,008 --> 00:21:44,011
A most fortuitous encounter
awaits you there.

475
00:21:45,888 --> 00:21:47,848
That's a very specific
instruction,

476
00:21:47,932 --> 00:21:49,600
plus you threw in a forecast.

477
00:21:49,683 --> 00:21:51,936
You feeling okay? Hit your head?

478
00:21:54,396 --> 00:21:57,358
[NOAH] Makoto, you are
the greatest apostle...

479
00:21:58,359 --> 00:22:01,070
And yet I haven't even
made use of you.

480
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:02,947
That day is still
quite a ways off.

481
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:04,532
[giggles]

482
00:22:05,074 --> 00:22:06,617
[♪ closing theme song playing]

